# The startup sequence (1280x800). The boot loader's splash stays as it is
# while the display's driver comes (QEMU's VGA is the driver VM's: Linux's
# bochs driver, with Veda's for Linux): the compositor draws nothing until
# its first picture, the splash as the loader painted it, is on the
# screen. Then the splash comes to life (the light around the ring, the
# name and the tagline), and once the desktop has drawn itself and the
# startup sound is ready (the sound card is the driver VM's too), it
# dissolves into the desktop as the sound starts.
sound hda
fail-on "PANIC"
wait-serial "compositor: the display's driver is coming" 120
wait-serial "compositor: the splash comes to life" 120
expect-serial "showing the compositor's frames"
wait 0.8
shot target/veda/startup-1-splash.png
wait-serial "compositor: the desktop appears" 60
wait-serial "shell: startup sound: playing" 10
wait-serial "compositor: desktop shown after" 60
wait 1
shot target/veda/startup-2-desktop.png
reject-serial "startup sound: no sound card"
reject-serial "no desktop after"
reject-serial "did not say the desktop may appear"
reject-serial "did not show its first picture"
expect-audio
expect-audio-gapless
